      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'Iemand wat die medisyne elke dag drink': The pronoun 'Sy' and 'soos enige ander kind' follow a genderless, ageless 'Iemand', so the reference is loose.",
        "fix: [taal] in 'Jy kan naby haar wees en jy kan haar druk sonder gevaar.': Missing AWS comma between two full clauses (jy kan wees / jy kan druk).",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Dit beteken nie dat elke mens met MIV VIGS sal kry nie.': The two abbreviations stand side by side ('MIV VIGS') and a Grade 4 reader may stumble; a fix such as 'elke mens wat MIV het, VIGS sal kry' adds a word, and the study text may not get longer, so it is flagged rather than changed.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Iemand wat met MIV leef, kan jou maat of jou klasmaat wees. Dit kan jo': 'haar' refers back to the gender-neutral 'Iemand' / 'jou onderwyser'; standard generic reference would be 'hom', but the female pronoun may be a deliberate choice (the medicine block also uses 'sy'), so it is not changed.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Wanneer MIV die liggaam se afweer teen siekte baie swak gemaak het.': The definition opens with 'Wanneer', so it names a time rather than a thing; the study text frames it as 'die naam vir wat gebeur wanneer ...'. A fix lengthens the entry, so it is flagged for the reviewer or writer."
      ]
